  message: "DONE 2026-09-06 (PR #802), the python leg of WI-lutuh's order, sequenced as this item's own rule asks: rows first, grants after.\n\nINSTRUMENT: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/dupok_python_09062026/ -- probe_py.py (public members one level deep; inspect.getsource scanned for open( / os. / sys.std* / socket; NATIVE opaque; never grants), probe_py.out/.json, PLAN.md (pre-registered), arm.sh/compare_arms.py A/B. Working set: the 41 stdlib module strings the 08-24 scope audit found uncatalogued across 11 repos (lutuh_scope raw.json minus the 77 grants).\n\nROWS ADDED (recall that stands on its own): glob.glob/iglob (fs_read); mimetypes init/read_mime_types/guess_type + MimeTypes.read/readfp; filecmp cmp/cmpfiles + dircmp.report*; sysconfig config-file readers (fs_read) + get_platform (env_read); cProfile.run/runctx + Profile.dump_stats (fs_write; an earlier draft also declared them fs_read and the mode-parity gate refused the dual: a read+write pair with no mode argument is a mode-decided primitive no analyzer can settle) + Profile.print_stats (logging); pstats.Stats load_stats (fs_read) / dump_stats (fs_write) / print_* (logging); xml.dom.minidom.parse (fs_read), xml.dom.getDOMImplementation (env_read); unittest.main / TextTestRunner.run (logging), TestLoader.discover (fs_read); optparse OptionParser.print_*/error/exit (logging), Values.read_file/read_module; doctest.testfile (fs_read), testmod / run_docstring_examples / DocTestRunner.run/summarize (logging); pprint.pprint/pp + PrettyPrinter.pprint; traceback print_* + TracebackException.print; codecs.open (dual fs_read+fs_write, builtins.open's shape); ctypes.CDLL/PyDLL/OleDLL/WinDLL, cdll.LoadLibrary, ctypes.util.find_library (fs_read; INV-buzab's live false confirm); multiprocessing.Process.start + Pool (subprocess), Process.kill/terminate (ipc_send); socket.create_connection (net_send), create_server (net_listen); ssl: SSLSocket send*/write/connect*/do_handshake (net_send), recv*/read/accept (net_recv), SSLObject read/write, ssl.get_server_certificate (net_recv), SSLContext.load_cert_chain/load_verify_locations/load_dh_params/load_default_certs (fs_read).\n\nGRANTS (44, dated 2026-09-06, each note names the probe verdict): errno, xml, xml.etree, xml.dom, xml.dom.minidom, glob, mimetypes(+MimeTypes), filecmp(+dircmp), sysconfig, pprint(+PrettyPrinter), traceback(+TracebackException), threading, cProfile(+Profile), pstats(+Stats), struct, binascii, operator, marshal, zlib, decimal, enum, string, atexit, queue, pickle, codecs, ctypes(+util), optparse(+OptionParser,+Values), doctest(+DocTestRunner), unittest(+TestLoader,+TextTestRunner), multiprocessing.Process, multiprocessing.Pool.\n\nREFUSED, written in the yaml: tkinter (display I/O, out of scope); socket (DNS functions unruled in every catalogue -> WI-dozul-pazoj-kimot-kamoz-romub-jofid-kipit-rihim, owner's call); ssl (rowed, PARTIAL: descriptor plumbing and MemoryBIO not read one by one); unittest.mock; multiprocessing (Manager / shared_memory / connection not read).\n\nGATES THAT FOLLOWED THE ROWS: `exit` added to ambiguous_names (optparse.OptionParser.exit vs the builtin); multiprocessing.Process.start + Pool added to HIGH_RISK_PRIMITIVES (WI-sugav drift guard); CATALOGUE_SCOPE['python'] extended by the 33 new stdlib modules with reasoning; the INV-buzab examined-negative fixtures ctypes and socket.create_connection GRADUATED (both classify now) and are repointed at termios and socket.gethostbyname, the graduated ones kept as positive controls.\n\nRULES APPLIED from the 08-15 survey: a read from a caller-opened object is the caller's I/O (pickle.load, marshal.load, minidom.parse(fileobj): no row); a write into one is rowed where the value enters it (pickle.dump keeps fs_write, json.dump's precedent). Pinned in test_python_completeness_third_leg.py.\n\nA/B (five-repo python cohort: httpx, full-stack-fastapi-template, poetry, django, hypergumbo self; cold caches; NO-NET / NO-FSWRITE / NO-FSREAD / NO-SUBPROC):\n  0 of 20 verdict categories moved. Surviving inconclusive, both arms: full-stack-fastapi-template NO-NET / NO-SUBPROC (\"supported language(s) javascript were analyzed but produced no call edges\"), httpx NO-SUBPROC (7 opaque launches: ./scripts/sync-version, git, grep, head, rm ...). Every other claim violated in both arms.\n  THE ROWS ARE VISIBLE AS RECALL in the violated claims' chain counts: django NO-FSREAD 606 -> 638, NO-SUBPROC 23 -> 24; hypergumbo NO-FSREAD 2016 -> 2026; poetry NO-FSREAD 205 -> 208; httpx NO-FSREAD 7 -> 9 (glob / mimetypes / sysconfig / codecs.open / TestLoader.discover reads, a multiprocessing launch). Not read back one by one: they are additions to already-violated claims, the direction that reports more.\n  The grants' positive control is TestTheGrantsPermitACleanVerdict (a call into struct is adjudicable; tkinter and httpx still withhold). compare.out in the instrument dir."  # 6097
